# Sell.do Backend API Discovery

## Sources (run `npm run refs:sync`)
- Rails: `.refs/crm`, branch `origin/feature-crm-2.0-dev`, **no working tree** (Windows-invalid file names). Read with:
  - `git -C .refs/crm show origin/feature-crm-2.0-dev:config/routes.rb`
  - `git -C .refs/crm ls-tree -r --name-only origin/feature-crm-2.0-dev | rg <name>`
  - `git -C .refs/crm grep -n "<text>" origin/feature-crm-2.0-dev -- app/controllers`
- App: `.refs/crm-flutter/lib/core/constants/api_endpoints.dart` lists every path the app calls; `lib/features/*/data/network/*_api_service.dart` shows params.

## Reading order for any feature
1. App side: which endpoint the screen calls (`api_endpoints.dart` -> `*_api_service.dart` -> repository).
2. `config/routes.rb` (legacy) or `config/routes/v3_routes.rb` (Api::V3) -> controller#action.
3. Controller: `before_action`s (auth/api_key), strong params, rendered JSON keys.
4. Model/service validations -> required vs optional; client-config flags that change them.
5. Write/extend a typed method in `src/api/`, with the route + `Controller#action` in its doc comment.

## Hosts & auth
| Domain in config | api_key host | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `v2.sell.do` | `https://v2.sell.do` | staging; v2a/v2b share this DB |
| `v2b.sell.do` | `https://v2.sell.do` | v2b serves Next UI; legacy JSON 404s there; `/api/v3/*` needs JWT + `X-Selldo-Request` |
| `app.sell.do` | `https://app.sell.do` | production |

- **Full-access key** (`api_key` + `client_id` query): `/client/*.json` (users, leads, config) and full lead JSON from `retrieve_lead`.
- **Restricted/website key**: never stored - `ClientConfigApi.websiteApiKey()` pages through `GET /client/api_clients.json` (15 per page, `total`) and takes the oldest client with `category: "restricted"` and `api_client_type: "website"`. Other restricted types (housing_pusher, facebook_puller, ...) return 200 from `/api/leads/create` but create nothing. Used for `POST /api/leads/create` only (body `{ api_key, sell_do: { form: { lead: {...} } } }`); with it `retrieve_lead` returns only `id`/`email`/`phone` (no names, stage, campaign), so always verify with the full-access key.
- `/api/v3/*` (CRM 2.0): Bearer JWT from `POST /api/v3/users/login` - not usable with api keys.

## Endpoints in use
| Purpose | Route | Controller#action | Key |
|---|---|---|---|
| Users listing (role filter) | `GET /client/users.json?search_params[role]=&search_params[department]=&search_params[status]=true` | `Client::UsersController#index` | full |
| Lead create (setup) | `POST /api/leads/create` | `Api::LeadsController#create` | restricted |
| Incoming email creates a lead | `POST /client/:client_id/mails/mailgun/incoming_mail` (form: `recipient` campaign mailbox, `sender`, `from` `Name <email>`, `To`, `subject`, `body-html`, `body-plain`, `Date`, `Message-Id`, `timestamp`, `token`, `attachment-count`) | `Client::Mails::MailgunController#incoming_mail` -> `IncomingMailLogObserver` | none (Mailgun). Answers `ok` even when the save is skipped; confirm with `retrieve_lead` |
| Send email | `POST /api/v3/client/leads/:id/emails` (`email.subject`, `email.html_content`, `email.toaddr` email-address ids, `email.email_template_type`, `email.email_template_id` when a template is chosen) | `Api::V3::Client::Leads::EmailsController#create` -> `V3::Leads::Emails::Create` | owner JWT |
| Reply / reply all | Same create, plus `email.in_reply_to` and, for reply all, `email.toCC`. Prefill is `GET .../emails/:email_id` (`subject`, `fromaddr`, `toaddr`, `toCC`, `direction`) and `GET .../emails/new` | `EmailsController#show` and `#screen`. Reply leaves CC empty. Reply all copies `toCC` | owner JWT |
| Email templates | `GET /api/v3/client/leads/:id/activity_lookups?type=email_templates` then `type=email_template&template_id=` (`subject`, `content`) | `ActivityLookupsController#index` | owner JWT |
| Email body | `GET /client/leads/:id/emails/:email_id` HTML (`<legend>` subject, then `html_content`). Activities JSON keeps subject, direction, toCC, and `email_template_id`, and omits the body | `Client::Leads::EmailsController#show` | full key |
| Read emails | `GET /client/leads/:id/activities.json?filters[_type]=Email` | activities feed | full key |
| Lead retrieve | `GET /api/leads/:type/retrieve_lead?value=` (type `email`/`phone`) | `Api::LeadsController#retrieve_lead` -> `process_lead_data` | full |
| App login | `POST /mobile/create.json` (`user[email]`, `user[password]`, `device_type`) | `MobileController#create` | UI |
| App lead save (v3 build) | `POST /api/v3/client/leads` (Bearer JWT, nested `lead` JSON) | `Api::V3::Client::LeadsController#create` -> `V3::Leads::Create` | UI |
| v3 sign-in | `POST /api/v3/users/login` on `settings.v3ApiBaseUrl` (staging: `https://v2a.sell.do`; v2 and v2b do not serve it) | `Api::V3::Users::SessionsController#create` | API |
| Schedule site visit | `POST /api/v3/client/leads/:id/site_visits` | `V3::Leads::SiteVisits::Create` | UI or API |
| Site visit status | `PATCH /api/v3/client/site_visits/:id/status` (`conducted`, `dropped` = not interested) | `V3::SiteVisits::UpdateStatus` | UI or API |
| Reschedule site visit | `PATCH /api/v3/client/site_visits/:id` (status stays `scheduled`) | `V3::Leads::SiteVisits::Update` | UI or API |
| Read site visits | `GET /client/leads/:id/activities.json?filters[_type]=SiteVisit` | activities feed | full key |
| Follow-up form | `GET /api/v3/client/leads/:id/followups/new` (type, timezone, required custom fields, `options.cancellation_reasons`) | `client/leads/followups#screen` | sales JWT |
| Schedule follow-up | `POST /api/v3/client/leads/:id/followups` (`followup_type`, `scheduled_on` UTC `yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm`, `subject`, `agenda`) | `client/leads/followups#create` | UI or API |
| Follow-up status | `PATCH /api/v3/client/followups/:id/status` (`conducted`, or `cancelled` plus `cancellation_reason`) | `client/followup_statuses#update` | UI or API |
| Follow-up note | `PATCH /api/v3/client/followups/:id` (`cancellation_note`) | `client/followups#update` | UI or API |
| Read follow-ups | `GET /client/leads/:id/activities.json?filters[_type]=Followup` | activities feed | full key |
| Schedule clashes | `GET /api/v3/client/leads/:id/scheduled_events` (`type`, `scheduled_on`, `ends_on`) | `Api::V3::Client::Leads::ScheduledEventsController#index` | sales JWT |
| Open follow-ups / site visits | `GET /api/v3/client/lead/activities?type=Followup\|SiteVisit&segment=scheduled\|pending` | `Api::V3::Client::Lead::ActivitiesController#index` | sales JWT |
| Read feeds | `GET /client/leads/:id/activities.json?filters[_type]=Feed` (`feed_type` `stage_change`, `reassign`, `push_to_sales`, `lead_updated`) | activities feed | full key |
| Lead detail (access) | `GET /api/v3/client/leads/:id` (`isMine`, `actions`, `access_messages`) | `Api::V3::Client::LeadsController#show` | user JWT |
| Change stage | `GET` then `PATCH /api/v3/client/leads/:id/stage` (`stage`, `status`, `reason` for lost/unqualified) | `Api::V3::Client::LeadStagesController#new/#update` | owner JWT |
| Bulk stage form | `GET /api/v3/client/lead_bulk_stage_changes/new` (`pipelines[].stages`, drop-off `reasons`, booked excluded) | `Api::V3::Client::LeadBulkStageChangesController#new` | user JWT |
| Bulk stage change | `POST /api/v3/client/lead_bulk_stage_changes` (`lead_ids`, `stage`, `stage_role`, `status`, `reason`) | `#create` -> `BulkModifyLeadsStageWorker` | user JWT |
