| Reassign one lead | `PUT /api/v3/client/leads/:id/reassign` (`team_id` or `project_id`, `sales_id`, `reassignment_reason`) | `Api::V3::Client::Leads::ReassignmentsController#update` | owner JWT |
| Bulk reassign | `POST /api/v3/client/lead_bulk_reassignments` (`lead_ids`, `reassignment_strategy` `simple_reassignment` or `shuffle_reassignment`, `sales_ids`, `team_ids` or `project_id`) | `Api::V3::Client::LeadBulkReassignmentsController#create` -> `LeadBulkActionWorker` | user JWT |
| Push to sales | `POST /api/v3/client/leads/:id/push_to_sales` (`team_id` or `project_id`, `sales_id`) | `Api::V3::Client::Leads::SalesPushesController#create` -> `PushToSales.perform` | pre-sales JWT |
| Reassign strategy | `GET`/`PATCH /api/v3/client/client_configuration` `values.reassign_lead_strategy` `team` or `project` | `Api::V3::Client::ClientConfigurationsController#show/#update` | admin JWT |
| Push strategy | `GET /api/v3/client/pre_sales_configuration` (`push_lead_strategy`, `auto_forward`) | `Api::V3::Client::PreSalesConfigurationsController#show` | admin JWT |
| Lookups | `GET /api/v3/client/users/lookups`, `GET /api/v3/client/leads/lookups?type=salutations` | v3 lookups | user JWT |
| Pre-sales stages | `GET /client/configuration/data_provider_presales_stage.json` | `Client::ConfigurationController#data_provider_presales_stage` | full |
| App lead save (develop build) | `POST /client/leads.json?user_email=&user_token=` | `Client::LeadsController#create` | UI |

Match the app branch to the installed build (`.refs/crm-flutter`, see `scripts/sync-refs.ts`). Known contract gap (19 Nov 2026): `V3::Leads::Create` reads `lead.phones_attributes[]` / `lead.emails_attributes[]`, the v3 app sends `lead.primary_phone` / `lead.primary_email`, so app-created leads fail with "both email and phone of lead can't be blank".

Known contract gap (19 Nov 2026): before creating or rescheduling a site visit the app calls `GET /api/v3/client/activities/scheduled_events`. That path is not in `config/routes/v3_routes.rb` and returns 404 `{ "error": "Template not found" }`, so the app never reaches the create or reschedule call. `PATCH /api/v3/client/site_visits/:id` itself returns 200. Status changes (`dropped`, `conducted`) do not call the missing route. Follow-up create catches that lookup failure and still saves. The working clash lookup is `GET /api/v3/client/leads/:id/scheduled_events` (sales JWT). The suite calls that, plus the activity lists, and marks every open follow-up and site visit in the slot conducted before a test schedules.

Known contract gap (23 Nov 2026): Cancel follow-up loads reasons from `GET /api/v3/workflows/lookups?type=followup_cancellation_reasons`, which returns 403 Forbidden for the sales user. The same reasons are already on `GET /api/v3/client/leads/:id/followups/new` under `options.cancellation_reasons`. The cancel screen does not read them from there.

Known contract gap (23 Nov 2026): Edit lead sends `lead.secondary_emails[]` / `lead.secondary_phones[]` (`lead_form.dart` `toFields`). `V3::Leads::Update` only reads `lead.emails_attributes[]` / `lead.phones_attributes[]`, so a secondary email or phone added in the app is not stored. Name and salutation go through `write_scalars` and are stored.

Known contract gap (23 Nov 2026): Log offline call sends `{ offline_call: { direction, status, created_at, duration, notes } }` (`offline_call_form.dart` `toV3Json`). `V3::Client::Leads::OfflineCallParams` reads those keys at the top level and reads the time from `called_at`, not `created_at`. The create service then answers 422 `Direction is required. Status is required. Date and time are required.` A successful save stores missed calls as `not_answered` and answered calls as `answered`, with duration in seconds.

Known contract gap (23 Nov 2026): Add conducted site visit posts `{ site_visit: { status: conducted, conducted_on, notes, scheduled_on } }` (`conducted_site_visit_form.dart` `toV3Json`) to `POST /api/v3/client/leads/:id/site_visits`. `V3::Leads::SiteVisits::Create` drops `status`, `conducted_on` and `notes` and calls `ScheduleSiteVisit`, so the visit is validated as scheduled. A conducted time in the past is then rejected with `Scheduled on cannot be in the past for a scheduled site visit.`

Lost and unqualified require an enabled drop-off reason (`reasons` on the stage form, label "Stage change reason"). The stage-change feed is `Lead Stage was changed from {old name} ({Sales|Pre-Sales}) to {new name} ({Sales|Pre-Sales}).` and appends `Reason: {label}` for those two stages. Bulk stage change answers `Bulk Lead Stage Change started in background. It will be reflected soon.` and the worker skips a lead whose stage does not change, so an incoming lead cannot be bulk-changed to incoming.

Push to sales (`PushToSales.perform`) rejects the lead when `currently_in == sales` ("Lead is already in sales."), when `stage == incoming` ("Please contact and validate the lead before pushing it to sales."), or when it has no current project ("Please add project(s) of interest before pushing the lead to sales."). `pre_sales.push_lead_strategy` `project` sends `project_id`; anything else sends `team_id`. `auto_forward` hides the sales person and rejects a manual `sales_id`.

`Lead#is_mine` is false for a sales or pre-sales user who is not the primary or secondary owner, unless team-based access or an allied user grants it. The lead detail `actions.edit` flag is that `isMine` value. Reassign strategy `team` shows a Team field; `project` shows a Project field (`client_configuration.reassign_lead_strategy`).

## Data providers (full-access key, verified on v2 staging)
Resolve client configuration here instead of storing it. Most return `[{ id, text }]`; `text` is what the app shows.

| Data | Route |
|---|---|
| API clients / website key | `GET /client/api_clients.json?page=N` -> `{ total, results: [{ api_key, category, api_client_type, created_at }] }` |
| Campaigns | `GET /client/campaigns/data_provider.json` |
| Campaign email mailboxes | `GET /client/campaigns/data_provider_medium_values.json` (rows whose `text` contains `@`; plus-aliases excluded). `id` is the mailbox used as incoming-mail `recipient` |
| Sales stages | `GET /client/configuration/data_provider_sales_stage.json` |
| Pre-sales stages | `GET /client/configuration/data_provider_presales_stage.json` |
| Sales / pre-sales statuses | `GET /client/configuration/data_provider_sales_status.json`, `..._presales_status.json` |
| Sources | `GET /client/configuration/data_provider_for_source.json` |
| Teams | `data_provider_for_teams` - route not yet confirmed (`/client/teams/data_provider_for_teams.json` is 404); find its parent resource in `config/routes.rb` before use |

For any other entity: `git -C .refs/crm show origin/feature-crm-2.0-dev:config/routes.rb | rg data_provider`, read the action, confirm the response with one GET, then add a typed method to `src/api/`. If no provider exists, create the record via API in the test's Arrange step.

`retrieve_lead` (full key) returns `{ exists, lead: { id, first_name, last_name, name, email, phone (national), stage_data{id,value}, last_campaign{id,name}, sales_id, ... }, sales_details{id,name,team} }`. Compare stage and campaign by id (`stage_data.id` = stage provider `id`, `last_campaign.id` = campaign provider `id`); names differ in case (`"organic"` vs provider `"Organic"`).

## Rules
- Use the API for setup and verification; use the UI for the behaviour under test.
- GETs may retry; creates never retry (`HttpClient.post` is single-shot).
- Never print keys: go through `HttpClient` (redacts). Keys come only from `settings.credentials`.
